Upstream: https://github.com/memononen/nanosvg
Commit: 239e102ec2c691f2902e20ace2ed36ee4a35cfe6

Local changes (marked as altered per the zlib license):

- nanosvg.h, nsvg__parseStyle: right-trim each style entry with an exclusive
  end and skip empty entries. Upstream starts the trim at the terminator and
  then steps one byte past it, so the last entry of a style string (or an
  empty one) makes nsvg__parseNameValue read past the end of the buffer.
  Found by AddressSanitizer on stock Papirus icons.

- nanosvgrast.h, nsvg__addActive and nsvg__curveDivs: clamp float-to-int
  conversions. Nearly horizontal edges make NSVG__FIX*dxdy exceed INT_MAX, and
  converting that is undefined behavior (seen on 46 stock Papirus and Breeze
  icons under -fsanitize=float-cast-overflow); absurd stroke sizes overflow the
  curve division count the same way.
